// PROBE TEMPLATE -- 5 no-evidence probes for gate G8.
//
// Copy this file to probes.jsonl, then fill in `question` and `answer` for each line
// by opening the cited page. `answer` is deliberately null: validate_gold.py fails on
// "an answerable question needs a non-empty answer" until a person has read the page.
// A placeholder string would have passed, which is why there isn't one.
//
// WHAT A PROBE IS. G8 runs these with retrieval forced empty. The question IS
// answerable from the filings; the harness withholds the evidence, and the system must
// refuse rather than answer from what it memorised in pretraining. So a probe only
// tests anything if the model plausibly knows the figure already -- these are the
// headline numbers of three well-known issuers, chosen to be as tempting as possible.
//
// WHY THE ANSWER IS STILL RECORDED. With the true answer present, error analysis
// separates three outcomes: refused correctly, answered wrongly, and -- the worst case,
// invisible without it -- answered *correctly* with no evidence at all.
//
// Lines beginning with // are skipped by load_gold(), so this commentary is safe to keep.
//
// Pages come from `uv run python scripts/make_worklist.py --for probe`
// (data/evaluation/worklist/probe.jsonl carries the excerpts).
//
// HOW TO READ THE PAGE:
//     uv run python scripts/render_pages.py --from-probes
// then open the PNGs in results/runs/pages/. Read the figure off the image. Do NOT read
// it off any text this repository extracts: the extractor is the thing under test, so a
// digit it misreads would become a wrong gold answer that the candidate -- running the
// same extractor -- reproduces and is scored correct for (D-016).
//
// page_numbers are PDF POSITIONS, not printed page labels. That is what the parser emits
// and what the G4 citation gate compares against; a printed label here would fail every
// citation check, and the failure would be misread as the model citing wrongly.
//
// question_type is narrative_fact throughout: it routes to `narrative`, which is where
// an unguarded model would answer from memory, and it needs only page evidence. Change
// it to table_cell if you would rather cite the cell -- that then requires a tolerance
// and either a bbox or a structured_source_key.
//
// After filling in:  uv run python scripts/validate_gold.py --set probe
//                    uv run python scripts/check_leakage.py

